## Use it

### Claude Code

```bash
claude mcp add <%= it.name %><% for (const v of it.secretVars) { %> -e <%= v.name %>=…<% } %> -- <%= it.run.command %> <%= it.run.args.join(" ") %>
```

### Claude Desktop

Add to `claude_desktop_config.json` (Settings → Developer → Edit Config):

```json
<%~ JSON.stringify({ mcpServers: { [it.name]: { command: it.run.command, args: it.run.args, ...(it.secretVars.length ? { env: Object.fromEntries(it.secretVars.map((v) => [v.name, "…"])) } : {}) } } }, null, 2) %>
```

### Cursor

Add the same block to `.cursor/mcp.json` (project) or `~/.cursor/mcp.json` (global).

### Remote (Streamable HTTP)

```bash
MCP_TRANSPORT=http PORT=3000 MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=change-me <%= it.run.command %> <%= it.run.args.join(" ") %>
# endpoint: http://localhost:3000/mcp  (legacy SSE clients: MCP_TRANSPORT=sse → /sse)
```

A `Dockerfile` is included for container platforms such as Google Cloud Run (listens on `$PORT`, scales to zero).
